  "concise_summary": "A condensed summary entry identifying \"Zebra\" with the Hindu *Brahman* and reading 3-74 as the lifting of the veil of *Maya* to disclose the identity of Atman (inner self) and Brahman (world-mind) — *Tat Tvam Asi*, \"That Thou Art.\" Dick frames ordinary human life as bondage to *Karma* (deterministic pre-programming) overridden in 3-74 by Noös (Thinking Mind), so that the \"ruling monad\" of Absolute Mind replaced his ego and moved him from \"becoming\" to \"being.\" He likens his phosphene visions and 3rd-eye activity to the opening of a chakra in *Kundalini Yoga*, and casts Brahman as a voluntary Bodhisattva who descended into creation, \"forgot\" itself to share human fate, and now wakes up by regaining memory in humans.",
